NAME
    gcloud alpha biglake hive databases - manage BigLake Hive databases

SYNOPSIS
    gcloud alpha biglake hive databases COMMAND [GCLOUD_WIDE_FLAG ...]

DESCRIPTION
    (ALPHA) Manage BigLake Hive databases.

GCLOUD WIDE FLAGS
    These flags are available to all commands: --help.

    Run $ gcloud help for details.

COMMANDS
    COMMAND is one of the following:

     create
        (ALPHA) Creates a BigLake Hive database.

     delete
        (ALPHA) Deletes a BigLake Hive database.

     describe
        (ALPHA) Describes a BigLake Hive database.

     get-iam-policy
        (ALPHA) Get the IAM policy for a BigLake Hive catalog database.

     list
        (ALPHA) List BigLake Hive databases in a catalog.

     set-iam-policy
        (ALPHA) Set the IAM policy for a BigLake Hive catalog database.

     update
        (ALPHA) Updates a BigLake Hive database.

NOTES
    This command is currently in alpha and might change without notice. If this
    command fails with API permission errors despite specifying the correct
    project, you might be trying to access an API with an invitation-only early
    access allowlist.

